  "_schema": "phantasie.graphics-pack/v1",
  "_note": "Apple II Phantasie III art (tools/scripts/extract_a2_p3_graphics.py + build_a2_p3_asset_manifest.py, reverse-engineering/apple2/phantasie3/GRAPHICS.md). Monsters are MONSTER SHAPES sprites (raw hi-res bytes, drawn by MONSTER PLOT at an odd byte column, as the game); party figures, map tiles and dungeon marks are Applesoft shapes (SHAPES) at the game's HCOLOR; colour is an NTSC artifact model [~]. The title and the ending's gods' room come only from an original copy: the [cr] copy's ICE DRAGON and WIN PIC are the cracker's screens. Text: the remaster 5x7 font (the Apple's hi-res font, IMPTEXT, lacks '.', '!', '/' and more; it is in font/). Screen kept at the remaster's 320 x 200 layout: Apple pictures (280 x 192) are drawn 1:1 in it.",
